From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi/phy: initialize PLL bias when enabling the PHY

PHY enable establishes a PLL bias reference and sets the power bits, but
leaves PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES uninitialized. Subsequent bias gets skip the
register writes because the reference is already held, including the
slave bias get during bonded PLL prepare.

Initialize PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES while establishing the PHY reference and allow
the bias to settle before continuing. The existing reference stays held
across host power on, so temporary clock operations cannot power down the
PLL and lose its register contents.

Fixes: cb55f39bf7b1 ("drm/msm/dsi/phy: Fix reading zero as PLL rates when unprepared")
Link: https://git.kernel.org/torvalds/c/cb55f39bf7b1e687b88dc9825c21a7d3454b5acb
Link: https://www.mail-archive.com/dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org/msg638716.html
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -1096,7 +1096,9 @@
 	data = DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_DIGTOP_PWRDN_B |
 	       DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_PLL_SHUTDOWNB;
 	writel(data, base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
+	writel(0xc0, phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
+	ndelay(250);
 
 	/* Assert PLL core reset */
 	writel(0x00, base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_PLL_CNTRL);
